---
onetaskgraph_template: 1
description: >-
  The planning workflow for one brief, as a plan graph: a plan its run has started is first
  refreshed from the run's current state, the planner drafts the plan, any
  spikes it needs run and a planner finalizes the plan from their reports, the plan is
  checked and reviewed, its design document is written,
  plan and document are copied onto the board, and the run waits for the user's approval.
  `just plan <brief>` creates it and launches it in one flow.
variables:
  plan:
    description: The qualified id of the plan project the planner writes, `authoring:<native id>`, from the brief's `Plan project:` line.
    type: text
    required: true
  native:
    description: The plan project's native id, the part of `plan` after its source.
    type: text
    required: true
  plan_title:
    description: The plan's title, the brief's H1, which the plan project is titled with.
    type: text
    required: true
  brief:
    description: The path of the manager's brief, as the recipe was given it.
    type: text
    required: true
  brief_text:
    description: The brief's whole text.
    type: text
    required: true
  checklist:
    description: The plan checklist's rules, as `llmlint rules -c config/plan-checklist.llmlint.yml --files <hypothetical plan paths> --format markdown` prints them.
    type: text
    required: true
  destination:
    description: The configured source the reviewed plan and its design document are copied into.
    type: text
    default: plans
members:
  - id: "{{ native }}-planning-refresh"
    title: "Refresh {{ plan }} from its run's current state"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "`just refresh-plan` brings a plan copied to `{{ destination }}` to its run's current state: board statuses and live-added tasks in, run-written keys out. A plan with no copy there is left as it is."
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: refresh
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [just, refresh-plan, "{{ plan }}", "{{ destination }}"]
  - id: "{{ native }}-planning-draft"
    title: "Draft the plan {{ plan }}"
    template: {file: planning-draft.md.j2}
    answers:
      plan: "{{ plan }}"
      plan_title: "{{ plan_title }}"
      brief: "{{ brief }}"
      brief_text: "{{ brief_text }}"
      checklist: "{{ checklist }}"
      destination: "{{ destination }}"
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-planning-refresh"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: draft
      onepipeline.persona: ../personas/planner.yaml
      onepipeline.agent_graph: graphs/planner.yaml
  - id: "{{ native }}-planning-spikes"
    title: "Run the spikes of {{ plan }}, if it has any"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "`scripts/spike-records.sh run` runs the spikes of `{{ plan }}-spikes` whose definitions changed since they last ran, attached in this flow, and settles done at once when there are none."
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-planning-draft"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: spikes
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [scripts/spike-records.sh, run, "{{ plan }}"]
  - id: "{{ native }}-planning-finalize"
    title: "Finalize {{ plan }} from its spikes, if it has any"
    template: {file: finalize.md.j2}
    answers:
      plan: "{{ plan }}"
      native: "{{ native }}"
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-planning-spikes"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: finalize
      onepipeline.persona: ../personas/planner.yaml
      onepipeline.agent_graph: graphs/planner.yaml
  - id: "{{ native }}-planning-spike-evidence"
    title: "Record the spike evidence of {{ plan }}"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "`scripts/spike-records.sh record` records, on each task built on spikes, the spike definitions its evidence now reflects."
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-planning-finalize"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: spike-evidence
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [scripts/spike-records.sh, record, "{{ plan }}"]
  - id: "{{ native }}-planning-check"
    title: "Check {{ plan }} as its launch will load it"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "`onepipeline plan check` over the plan, with this host's install check and spike-evidence check registered."
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-planning-spike-evidence"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: check
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [env, "ORCHESTRATOR_PLAN={{ plan }}", scripts/onepipeline.sh, plan, check, "{{ plan }}", --check, orchestrator/host_adoption_check.py, --check, scripts/spike-evidence-check.sh]
  - id: "{{ native }}-planning-review"
    title: "Review {{ plan }}"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "`scripts/review-plan-item.sh` judges every unreviewed task and the project, and attests each pass."
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-planning-check"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: review
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [scripts/review-plan-item.sh, "{{ plan }}"]
  - id: "{{ native }}-planning-design"
    title: "Write the design document of {{ plan }}"
    template: {file: design.md.j2}
    answers:
      plan: "{{ plan }}"
      native: "{{ native }}"
      brief_text: "{{ brief_text }}"
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-planning-review"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: design
      onepipeline.persona: ../personas/design-doc.yaml
      onepipeline.agent_graph: graphs/design-doc.yaml
  - id: "{{ native }}-planning-copy"
    title: "Copy {{ plan }} and its documents to {{ destination }}"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "`onetaskgraph project copy` of the plan, its tasks and its documents, into `{{ destination }}`."
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-planning-design"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: copy
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [.venv/bin/onetaskgraph, project, copy, "{{ plan }}", --to, "{{ destination }}", --documents, --no-interactive]
  - id: "{{ native }}-planning-approve-design"
    title: "Approve the design of {{ plan }}"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "Waits for the user's approval of the design document on the board copy."
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-planning-copy"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: approve-design
      onepipeline.kind: human
      onepipeline.human_item:
        kind: task
        priority: medium
        title: "Read and approve the design for {{ plan }}"
        body: >-
          Read the design document of the copy of {{ plan }} in {{ destination }} (its id is
          the `onetaskgraph.copies` entry `onetaskgraph project show {{ plan }} --json`
          names). Once the user approves it, run `just approve-design <that copy>
          <this run's id>`.
---
The planning run of `{{ plan }}`, from the brief `{{ brief }}`: refresh, draft, spikes, finalize, spike evidence, check, review,
design document, copy to `{{ destination }}`, and the user's approval.
